NAME
       less - page through a file or a command's output

SYNOPSIS
       less [-N] [-S] [-R] [-F] [-X] [-i] [FILE...]
       COMMAND | less

DESCRIPTION
       less shows text one screen at a time and lets you move back and
       forward and search. It does not read the whole file first, so it opens
       big log files at once. man and journalctl use less to show their
       output.

   Keys
       Space, f, Page Down    one screen forward
       b, Page Up             one screen back
       Down, j, Enter         one line forward
       Up, k                  one line back
       g, <                   go to the start
       G, >                   go to the end
       /TEXT                  search forward for TEXT (a regular expression)
       ?TEXT                  search backward
       n, N                   the next match, the previous match
       &TEXT                  show only the lines that match
       -N                     turn line numbers on or off while reading
       F                      follow the end of a growing file (like
                              tail -f; Ctrl+C to stop)
       h                      help
       q                      quit

OPTIONS
       -N     Show line numbers.

       -S     Cut long lines instead of wrapping them (scroll with the left
              and right arrows).

       -R     Show colour codes as colours.

       -F     Quit at once if the text fits on one screen.

       -X     Leave the text on the screen after quitting.

       -i     Searches ignore case unless the search has capitals.

       -E     Quit at the end of the file.

       -M     A longer prompt with the position in the file.

EXAMPLES
       Read the system log and search for errors:

           less /var/log/messages
           /error

       Page through a long listing:

           ls -lR /etc | less

       Show a configuration file with line numbers:

           less -N /etc/ssh/sshd_config

SEE ALSO
       more(1), head(1), tail(1), man(1)
